                                   "title":  "The Garden of Words",
                                   "snippet":  "[MAL Review of The Garden of Words by Veronin, score 7/10]: Makoto Shinkai is a name that has become increasingly prevalent over the years. And for good reason, too. After hitting the anime industry in 2007 with his opus magnum \"5 Centimeters Per Second\", he quickly established himself as a director with the ability to combine masterful artistic talent with emotional, bittersweet storytelling. Does his latest animation achieve that same ideal? In some ways, it does. But if you are awaiting another great story, this is not what you are looking for. \"The G",
                                   "link":  "https://myanimelist.net/anime/16782"
                               },
                               {
                                   "title":  "The Garden of Words",
                                   "snippet":  "[MAL Review of The Garden of Words by Kirik0h, score 9/10]: The greatest injustice that can be inflicted upon “Kotonoha no Niwa” is to falsely and narrowly label this 46-minute film a simple story of love. Too often do you see people claim that this movie is one about a \"forbidden love\" created by an age difference and it is through these lens that unwarranted and confused criticisms of the show sometimes emerge. The Garden of Words has a level of nuanced complexity that is concealed for the presumptuous as it requires you to think and pay attention to i",
                                   "link":  "https://myanimelist.net/anime/16782"
                               },
                               {
                                   "title":  "The Garden of Words",
